# Yosys synthesis of the PPU to gf180mcu_fd_sc_mcu7t5v0.
#
# Replaces the "~40k gates / ~1.6 mm2" estimate in ip/ppu/README.md section 10
# with a measured number. Run via ip/ppu/scripts/synth.sh, which supplies
# PDK_ROOT and writes the reports.
#
# SRAM macros are blackboxed: they are hard macros with known LEF areas, so
# counting them as logic would double-count. Their area is added back in the
# report.
#
# USING THE CELLS THE LIBRARY ACTUALLY HAS
# ----------------------------------------
# mcu7t5v0 has 229 cells. Three of them change the result materially, and the
# original `synth; dfflibmap; abc` flow here used none of them:
#
#   icgtp/icgtn  integrated clock gates. This library has NO enable flop, so
#                every `if (en) q <= d` became a feedback mux2 -- 1282 of them,
#                13.6% of the logic area. mux2 is 28.5 um2 and icgtp is 61.5, so
#                a clock gate wins on any enabled register wider than two bits,
#                and most of them are far wider. MEASURED: -30 249 um2, -11.4%
#                of total logic. The single largest optimisation available here.
#   tieh/tiel    constants need a driver cell to be physically real. Without
#                them the constant-zero bits of `prdata` are left literally
#                undriven and `check` reports 24 of them as bugs.
#                MEASURED: +53 um2, and it is not optional.
#
# What is NOT worth doing, also measured rather than assumed:
#
#   addf/addh    the library has full and half adders and the netlist uses zero
#                of them, which looks like a missed opportunity and is not: a
#                gate-built full adder is xor3 (50.5) + carry (~28.5) = ~79 um2
#                against addf's 72.4. That is 8% on adder logic alone, and abc
#                already finds xor3/xnor3 for the sum terms. Not worth a custom
#                techmap to chase.
#   abc -D 20    ADOPTED, and the earlier "-D changes nothing" note was wrong
#                for an embarrassing reason: the first experiment passed 40000
#                assuming picoseconds, but abc's -D is in LIBRARY UNITS -- ns
#                here -- so it constrained the design to 40 microseconds, i.e.
#                not at all. At -D 20 abc restructures the deep xor3 arithmetic
#                (+2% area, 8569 cells) and pre-place STA at ss_125C_4v50 then
#                closes the 25 MHz games mode at +0.38 ns where the area-mode
#                netlist missed by -0.17. The HD framebuffer modes need a
#                mode-aware SDC besides (fb_en case analysis): every endpoint
#                failing at 37.125 MHz is render-path arithmetic that is idle
#                when the scanner drives the screen.
#   muxcover     `muxcover -mux4` LOOKED like a 1 128 um2 saving and is not: it
#                emits $_MUX4_ cells that nothing downstream maps, so 31 cells
#                left the flow with no area attributed to them at all and the
#                "saving" was the missing area. abc already picks mux4_1 out of
#                the liberty where it pays. Removed.
#   setundef     `-undriven` adds 481 tie cells (+3 872 um2) and fixes nothing:
#                `check`'s 189 undriven wires are hierarchical ALIASES left by
#                -flatten (u_display.vid_r and friends, whose drivers now sit on
#                the top-level port net), not real floating nodes. They are
#                present identically without any of these passes.
#
# DFT NOTE: `clockgate` ties each ICG's test-enable low, so scan cannot toggle
# a gated clock. A design entering a real DFT flow must drive those from
# scan-enable instead; the library has the scan flops (sdffq/sdffrnq/...) for
# when that day comes.

read_verilog -I rtl -DSYNTHESIS rtl/ppu_blend.v
read_verilog -I rtl -DSYNTHESIS rtl/ppu_timing.v
read_verilog -I rtl -DSYNTHESIS rtl/ppu_cache.v
read_verilog -I rtl -DSYNTHESIS rtl/ppu_unpack.v
read_verilog -I rtl -DSYNTHESIS rtl/ppu_cmd.v
read_verilog -I rtl -DSYNTHESIS rtl/ppu_scanbuf.v
read_verilog -I rtl -DSYNTHESIS rtl/ppu_fbscan.v
read_verilog -I rtl -DSYNTHESIS rtl/ppu_display.v
read_verilog -I rtl -DSYNTHESIS rtl/ppu_csr.v
read_verilog -I rtl -DSYNTHESIS rtl/ppu_top.v
read_verilog -lib scripts/sram_blackbox.v

hierarchy -check -top ppu_top

synth -top ppu_top -flatten

# Enable -> clock gate. Runs BEFORE dfflibmap, because it works on the generic
# $_DFFE_ cells; -liberty lets it choose the ICG out of the library itself.
clockgate -liberty @LIBERTY@

dfflibmap -liberty @LIBERTY@
abc -liberty @LIBERTY@ -D 20
opt_clean

# Constants need real drivers.
# tieh drives Z but tiel drives ZN -- gate-level simulation caught the Y-wiring as "port Y is
# not a port of _NNN_" where STA had only muttered a warning and moved on.
hilomap -hicell gf180mcu_fd_sc_mcu7t5v0__tieh Z -locell gf180mcu_fd_sc_mcu7t5v0__tiel ZN

setundef -zero
splitnets
opt_clean

tee -o reports/stat.txt stat -liberty @LIBERTY@
tee -o reports/check.txt check
write_verilog -noattr reports/ppu_synth.v
